  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "For which number theoretic functions $f$ is it true that, for any $F(n)$ such that $f(n)/F(n)\\to 0$ for almost all $n$, there are infinitely many $x$ such that $ \\frac{\\#\\{ n\\in \\mathbb{N} : n+f(n)\\in (x,x+F(x))\\}}{F(x)}\\to \\infty? $ ",
